    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0885" n="851" xml:id="pg851"/>

                <head>360. Telegram From the Mission to the European Communities to the Department
                    of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d360-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Brussels</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1967-12-07T17:46:00+00:00">December 7, 1967,
                        1746Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>3434. Pass Agriculture. Subject: Supplementary Poultry Levies.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Commission official informed us that at December 6 Management Committee
                        meeting no changes were recommended on the levies on turkeys or turkey
                        parts.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>He said that this lack of action should, in fact, be interpreted as action
                        favorable to United States’ interests, and we should recognize it as such.
                        His explanation was that the price information the Management Committee had
                        before it would have justified increased levies, e.g. an 80 percent increase
                        in the supplementary levy on whole turkeys of about 5 cents.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Source reiterated that Commission should be given recognition for action
                        it had taken which indicated that our views and representations had been
                        taken into account.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Source urged U.S. officials to hold this information, especially paragraph
                        2, closely and to use it with great discretion in order to avoid a situation
                        in which the Commission would be forced to impose the increases.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>We hope to obtain tomorrow details concerning other recommendations that
                        may have been made by Poultry Management Committee.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Schaetzel</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
